      "dc:source": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/sources/1487/",
      "target": {
        "source": {
          "id": "https://figgy.princeton.edu/concern/scanned_resources/2bf15442-396b-4669-9521-61f7de4ffa31/manifest/canvas/a1ecb7b7-b92e-4192-942b-1c4bb9974190",
          "type": "Canvas",
          "partOf": {
            "id": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/documents/5695/iiif/manifest/"
          }
        },
        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:554.7943725585938,1486.3936767578125,3166.1275024414062,4463.5692138671875",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Translated by Brendan G. Goldman.",
          "value": "<p>My advice, which, if you had borne in mind . . . give precedence to all these words of mine according to the strength of my grief and to . . . strong and the yearning for you far away in a city not . . . [and] not close and not . . . but you are there\u2014alone and by yourself. I, therefore, am unable to be patient.</p>\n<p>Your brother married off Qabalah and Yam\u0101na in Ragusa, and I am with them . . . in Ragusa. But from the day I married them off, my tears have not stopped out of my yearning for you. Your [other] brother, Ab\u016b Y\u016bsuf, I married off in Syracuse, and he wept [out of longing for] you. If you saw him, you would not recognize him, [so changed is he] from the depth of his longing for you . . .</p>\n<p>. . . three years we had no news while you were missing. We had a massive funeral for you. We cried over you[r loss], weeping for a man who died in a strange city where he had no friends, [where] no one knew him or cried over [his death]. Then this year your letter was read out loud to me! From the very hour of its reading, I felt . . . sorrow for your distance. I longed for your presence\u2014may God reunite us in the most auspicious of circumstances and best frame of mind.</p>\n<p>Right now, my son, I will make you swear by God that you will not spend more time away than you already have. I make you swear by God, my son, I pray, from the moment that you read my letters, you will make haste to come to me by any means before I die. I have not seen you nor been in your presence . . .</p>\n<p>Your father, may God have mercy on him, died when you were present. Take it to heart, bear in mind, awaken your spirit and say, \u201cMy father died\u00a0</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
